\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Remark}
\p{Note that the converse is not true, since, for example, #{T(n)} might be #{O(g(n))} even if the limit does not exist. As a counterexample, let #{T(n) = 0} when #{n} is even, and #{1} when #{n} is odd. Then #{T(n)} is #{O(1)} but #{\lim T(n)/1} does not exist. But typically this won’t be an issue with the functions we will see in this class!}


